WEBVTT

00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:14,820
I think it might have thyroid problems, what's the best test for that?

00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:24,820
Well, for thyroid issues, you, that's a standard lab test and you want to test for, um,

00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:30,740
do a thyroid panel, though, like, um, just going off the top of my head, I got to type

00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:35,300
some of those things in that you would test for.

00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:41,780
Typically, if you go into your doctor, you say, I want to have my thyroid test and they'll

00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:47,380
test for TSH, which is thyroid stimulating hormone. Well, thyroid stimulating hormone is actually

00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:53,460
produced by the pituitary gland, and it's basically telling the thyroid to release more formal.

00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:59,940
So if the thyroid stimulating hormone is elevated, that's a hint that you might have low thyroid.

00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:07,780
But that is so inconclusive. You don't just test TSH and then say you have thyroid

00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:13,380
hypothyroid issue. You have to test for the thyroid hormone. So what are the thyroid hormones?

00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:21,780
So you got T3. T3 is the active thyroid hormone, but it's really only, um, about 6% of what the

00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:29,860
thyroid gland produces. The thyroid gland really produces 94% T4. So T4 is not

00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:38,500
an active hormone state. It doesn't have any physical activity to any of the cells. T4 then

00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:47,220
converts to T3 in the liver and in the gut at a timely fashion. So when your body needs it over

00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:55,460
the course of the day, T4 will convert to T3. Well, problem is then you want to know how much

00:01:55,540 --> 00:02:04,180
free T3 and free T4 is. So you would also test for free T3 and you'd also test for free T4.

00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:12,180
And then you'd also test for a thing that's called reverse T3, because if you have a sick

00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:20,340
gut, then your T4 instead of converting to T3, it converts to this other compound that is

00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:25,860
inactive and can never become active. And that's called reverse T3. So you'll want to test for

00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:32,900
the percentage of reverse T3 you have, because you might have adequate T4, adequate T3, but you have

00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:40,820
very elevated T, reverse T3, and that's the side of thyroid issues, but gut issues and possibly

00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:48,660
liver issues. And then you also want to test for TPO antibodies, because that will tell you if you

00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:56,820
possibly have Hashimoto's. So that is a more complete thyroid panel. You really want to get,

00:02:56,820 --> 00:03:03,620
you know, when we order thyroid panels for people, we order them through lab core, and then we also

00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:12,100
get, you know, a CBC ad complete metabolic panel with that too, because we want to look at how the

00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:19,540
liver is doing, how the rest of the body is doing, how your blood is doing, that's your complete blood

00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:30,980
count, and your complete metabolic panel. That's a more appropriate thyroid function test.

